{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>My son shall not go down with you.</b> He remained silent here and did not answer him at all, and did not trust his words, because he had already offended against his father, and from now on he would not trust him. But he trusted the words of Judah, for Judah was mighty among his brothers, and his argument was: if you do not send our brother with us, and so forth; and if you do not send, and so forth. And so the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: Judah said to them, leave the old man alone until the bread is finished from the basket. Judah said: Father, if Benjamin goes with us, perhaps he will be seized, perhaps not; if he goes with us we shall live, and if he does not go with us we shall all die — better that you leave the doubtful and take the certain."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:57.946634521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}